usage: with_argbind.py [-h] [--args.save ARGS.SAVE] [--args.load ARGS.LOAD]
                       [--args.debug ARGS.DEBUG]
                       [--func.maybe_count FUNC.MAYBE_COUNT]
                       [--func.tags FUNC.TAGS] [--func.weights FUNC.WEIGHTS]
                       [--func.shape FUNC.SHAPE]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --args.save ARGS.SAVE
                        Path to save all arguments used to run script to.
  --args.load ARGS.LOAD
                        Path to load arguments from, stored as a .yml file.
  --args.debug ARGS.DEBUG
                        Print arguments as they are passed to each function.

Generated arguments for function func:
  Bind arguments annotated with modern (PEP 585 / PEP 604)
  syntax.

  --func.maybe_count FUNC.MAYBE_COUNT
                        An optional integer (PEP 604 union), by default None.
  --func.tags FUNC.TAGS
                        A list of strings, space-separated on the CLI, by default
                        None.
  --func.weights FUNC.WEIGHTS
                        A ``key=value`` mapping, by default None.
  --func.shape FUNC.SHAPE
                        A fixed-size tuple, by default (1, 2).
